[Chapter "Second-move deviations"]
[Line "Against the Petrov (2...Nf6)"]
[Opening "Petrov's Defense: Classical Attack"]

{Black counterattacks e4 instead of defending e5. Take e5, retreat, and take the centre.} 1. e4 {Take the centre.} 1... e5 2. Nf3 {Develop with an attack on e5.} 2... Nf6 {The Petrov: Black counterattacks e4.} 3. Nxe5 {Take the pawn. Black's best is 3...d6 first; copying with 3...Nxe4 runs into Qe2.} 3... d6 4. Nf3 {Retreat to a safe central square.} 4... Nxe4 5. d4 {Take the centre.} 5... d5 6. Bd3 {Develop and challenge the e4 knight.} *
